                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc9c0144-d679-3bc5-9828-e749e8c11655",
                        "entry_id": "85c2ca09-04ae-3fe7-910c-b2b94a4a9566",
                        "glosses": [
                            "betrekking hebbend op de aardplaten, de breuken in de aardplaten en hun verschuivingen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb894318-b11e-4fb7-804e-7d53fa6ca461",
                                "sense_id": "fc9c0144-d679-3bc5-9828-e749e8c11655",
                                "text": "Met de aardbeving in L'Aquila van 2009 nog vers in het geheugen, speelt zich momenteel 100 km ten noorden van de stad een gelijkaardig scenario af. De situatie in de Apennijnen in Centraal-Italië is volgens aardbevingsgeoloog Manuel Sintubin van de Universiteit in Leuven tektonisch gezien heel complex."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "520b7d88-ab00-491b-bfe3-9201e3e654dd",
                                "sense_id": "fc9c0144-d679-3bc5-9828-e749e8c11655",
                                "text": "De stad Los Angeles is bovenop de San Andreasbreuk gebouwd. Deze breuklijn vormt de overgang tussen twee tektonische platen die langs elkaar schuiven en aardbevingen veroorzaken. Wetenschappers vrezen al langer voor een catastrofale aardbeving."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "452df014-1ee5-46e0-8ee2-b0cf10f3a6ae",
                                "sense_id": "fc9c0144-d679-3bc5-9828-e749e8c11655",
                                "text": "Platentektoniek: De belangrijkste oorzaak van de bevingen zijn verschuivingen van aardplaten. \"Het gebied rond Voerendaal ligt in de Roerdalslenk, die wordt begrensd door twee grote breuken waardoor de ondergrond onder druk staat\", zegt Evers tegen 1Limburg. \"De regio staat tektonisch onder spanning. Die is te herleiden naar het Middellandse Zeegebied, waar vaker aardbevingen en vulkaanuitbarstingen voorkomen.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfbb31c0-05bd-4a2b-8ee7-26bdfe17e5e3",
                        "source_entry_id": "85c2ca09-04ae-3fe7-910c-b2b94a4a9566",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc9c0144-d679-3bc5-9828-e749e8c11655",
                        "source_sense_description": "betrekking hebbend op de aardplaten, de breuken in de aardplaten en hun verschuivingen",
                        "target_lang_word": "tectonic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tectonic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98e16c57-22db-3c71-bac4-da31b09e6fff",
                                        "entry_id": "0b6d97f2-ff3b-320c-a08c-ffbcbbfa9fd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to construction or to architecture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dc17b43-52ae-3cab-aa21-1a86476bcbbd",
                                        "entry_id": "0b6d97f2-ff3b-320c-a08c-ffbcbbfa9fd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Structural."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5eb38b5c-05fc-3733-bc99-e66ad850dc2c",
                                        "entry_id": "0b6d97f2-ff3b-320c-a08c-ffbcbbfa9fd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or caused by large-scale movements of the Earth's (or a similar planet's) lithosphere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16d66dfc-369c-45dc-a3ac-b9d62c377550",
                                                "sense_id": "5eb38b5c-05fc-3733-bc99-e66ad850dc2c",
                                                "text": "A boiling hot rock planet with extreme tectonic activity, Parnassus is home to many volcanic mountains. Surface scans reveal several geothermal and solar power stations, tapping the planet's abundant energy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9304a67-ed64-4850-9913-7cd3756bb649",
                                                "sense_id": "5eb38b5c-05fc-3733-bc99-e66ad850dc2c",
                                                "text": "At some point, Venus may have had its own form of plate tectonics – possibly different from the plate tectonics here on Earth. Water and rock measurements obtained from the DAVINCI mission, combined with the Venus global mapping information by NASA’s VERITAS mission, another recently selected mission to Venus that is managed by NASA’s Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Southern California, can be used to decipher how these tectonic patterns may have operated on Venus, and why the planet was unable to sustain them in a fashion similar to Earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b932584c-4777-31e9-b562-1cdc60294dd2",
                                        "entry_id": "0b6d97f2-ff3b-320c-a08c-ffbcbbfa9fd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Momentous, utter, vast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db2fc020-a378-4601-b7d3-cc3b1df530f9",
                                                "sense_id": "b932584c-4777-31e9-b562-1cdc60294dd2",
                                                "text": "But it would be a mistake to imagine that we are benignly coming full circle, or even that we are finding that the old ways are still the most efficient. A tectonic shift has occurred."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
